ook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI AKIYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA SHOUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIMURA TOMOYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, NAOYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUBARA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIROKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, AKIYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, SHOUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIMURA, TOMOYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A solution heat exchanger disposed in a solution flow channel in an absorption refrigerating machine and used for heat exchange between a dilute solution and a concentrated solution. The solutionheat exchanger (H) is a plate type heat exchanger and has a communication section (R) for providing, within the solution heat exchanger (H), communication between a dilute solution flow channel for introducing part of a dilute solution into a concentrated liquid and a concentrated solution flow channel.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un échangeur de chaleur pour solution placé dans une conduite d'écoulement de solution, d'une machine réfrigérante à absorption, et utilisé dans le but d'échanger de la chaleur entre une solution diluée et une solution concentrée. L'échangeur de chaleur (H) est un échangeur du type à plaques et possède une section de communication (R), située à l'intérieur de cet échangeur (H), destinée à permettre une communication entre une conduite d'écoulement de solution diluée, afin d'introduire une partie d'une solution diluée dans un liquide concentré, et une conduite d'écoulement de solution concentrée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>